ZREADER 0.8.1 — LOCAL BUILD / TEST REPORT
ARM static arm-linux-musleabihf / cortex_a53; MuPDF 1.28.6. Pause list unchanged:
awesome volumd blanket Xorg. Hardware dark mode untouched.

LIBRARY FLICKER — ROOT CAUSE
1. Every cover-cache revision (each disk read or generated cover) called
   markFull(REAGL): a separate full-screen update per arriving cover.
2. zr_thumbs_focus() demoted every READY RAM cover to "re-read from disk" on each
   page change, so even fully cached pages drew placeholders first, then
   repainted the whole screen again when the re-reads landed. It also discarded
   the next-page prefetch results.
3. The page was drawn immediately, before any cache read could finish.
4. zr_thumb() used trylock; a worker briefly holding the lock produced a
   spurious placeholder for a cached cover.

