FIX
- Ready covers stay ready across page changes; identity re-validation only on
  library rescan (off UI thread).
- Page change: request visible covers, then next and previous page (prefetch),
  hold up to 300 ms while disk reads finish, then ONE composed update.
- Covers still being generated: at most two batched GL16 PARTIAL updates limited
  to the union of thumbnail rectangles (batch 1 after all pending or 1.5 s,
  batch 2 when the rest finish). Never one update per cover.
- Blocking cover-cache lock (workers never hold it during I/O).
- Battery/storage are composed into the same raster; no separate updates.
- REAGL keeps the driver FULL update flag (as reader page turns do since v0.8);
  it is the non-flashing waveform, not a GC16 flash.

